{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01TKsgt2nH3FMFEZJGgSnnvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q18: What is re-ranking? Cross-encoder vs bi-encoder?**\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Concept:** Two-stage retrieve-then-rerank pipeline — bi-encoder for high-recall first-stage retrieval, cross-encoder for high-precision second-stage reordering on the top-N candidates only.\n- **Mechanism:** Bi-encoder encodes query and doc *independently* → ANN lookup (HNSW, pre-indexable, O(log N)); cross-encoder concatenates query+doc → full cross-attention → cannot pre-index, runs at query time only on top-50–200 candidates.\n- **Tools:** Cohere Rerank (managed, ~$1K/day at 1M QPS), BGE-Reranker-v2 (open-source), ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2 (lightweight).\n- **Concrete metric:** bi-encoder top-5 → hybrid top-50 + cross-encoder top-5 raised RAGAS context_precision from 0.61 → 0.82 (+34%), at cost of ~80ms p95 latency.\n- **Pitfalls:** Conflating re-ranking with \"running embeddings again\"; not mentioning two-stage structure; ignoring latency quantification.\n- **Cross-links:** Q17 (hybrid search feeds into reranking), Q21 (NDCG/MRR evaluate reranking quality), Q12 (sparse vs dense — bi-encoder is dense retrieval)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":60022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":367,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c347b03-c8e8-426c-9e26-30c0913512a7","uuid":"78ff6aac-5f2c-4eea-9762-66a2466e50ce"}
